 *
 * Business context: A soft-deleted post should not be visible to non-moderator members for both privacy and moderation audit reasons. However, moderators must retain the ability to view and possibly restore or investigate such posts. This test ensures that after a post is soft-deleted, it is only retrievable by an authorized moderator.
 *
 * Test Steps:
 * 1. Register a new member (who will later be a moderator)
 * 2. Assign moderator role to the new member
 * 3. Create a discussion category/thread context
 * 4. Create a new thread as the registered member
 * 5. Create a post in the new thread as the same member
 * 6. Soft-delete the post
